course: dictionary
lesson: 9197
title: Softball: a game and a ball
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a game and also the thing you use to play it. Softball is one of them. Read the words around it: «In baseball and softball the batter wears a helmet and drops the bat after hitting, never throwing it.» Softball sits next to baseball, so it is probably a similar game, and the batter, helmet and bat are clues that it is played with a bat.
explain: Softball can mean the game or the ball. «Play softball» means take part in the game, while «a softball» means one ball. Ask which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Softball is a team game, like baseball.
fact: Softball is played on a smaller field than baseball, with a bigger ball.
fact: In softball the ball is pitched underarm.
fact: Softball is very popular in the USA, Canada and Australia, in schools and parks.
fact: «Softball» is a noun. It is uncountable for the game, and «a softball» or «softballs» means the ball.
exercise: «In baseball and softball the batter wears a helmet and drops the bat after hitting, never throwing it.» What is softball? | A game played only with the feet | *A team game like baseball | A kind of cake eaten at lunch | A dance performed in a school hall
exercise: Find one word in the sentence that names a thing the batter holds. | helmet | after | *bat | softball
exercise: Sam says, «Pass me the softball!» What does softball mean here? | *The ball used in the game | A grassy field for picnics | A helmet worn by the batter | The team game itself
test: Compared with baseball, softball is played on a | bigger field | field made of water | field covered in snow | *smaller field
test: In softball, the ball is pitched how? | With a bat | *Underarm | Over the head with both hands | With the feet
exam: Which phrase means you are taking part in the game? | softball helmet | *play softball | softballs | a softball ball
